contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 7. Contract [1], for 14,990 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper activity. Similar trends could result from seasonal demand or budget cycles. Small amounts near the limit do not prove violations, as prices may naturally approach the threshold.\nWhat can be checked: Check the number of contracts per awardee to identify patterns. Review the dates and values of December contracts to see if they align with typical seasonal needs. Examine if multiple contracts cover the same service to avoid duplication.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["OxWP12LyCEuS81gZFETWmA%3D%3D","wRwDLwy4RETE6P%2FuLemXRw%3D%3D","0ga6ZhvOL2qP66GS%2BONYvQ%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-15"}}